L0118: Unknown built-in form

The compiler recognizes a fixed set of forms such as prop!, prove! and assert!. Arbitrary Rust macros are not expanded, and supported forms use their documented delimiters. Use the named Locus form or an ordinary function call.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/unknown_form.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```locus
// A form outside the closed list, one with brackets, one with braces, and
// `prove!` with two formulas.
fn first(n: u8) -> u8 {
    println!("{}", n);
    n
}

fn second(n: u8) -> u8 {
    let items = vec![1, 2];
    n
}

fn third(n: u8) -> u8 {
    todo!{}
}

fn fourth(n: u8) -> u8 {
    prove!(n == n, n == n);
    n
}
```

Language, as built: [1.6:1](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.6:1).
